---
// Required by Google for the "Jeeves YouTube" OAuth app (Google Cloud project jeeves-youtube-510115).
// Deliberately not linked from the nav, the footer or the sitemap, and marked noindex.
import RootLayout from "@/layouts/RootLayout.astro";
---

<RootLayout title="Privacy policy: Jeeves YouTube" description="How the Jeeves YouTube app uses YouTube data." noindex>
    <div class="section-container animate-fade-in">
        <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto py-16 space-y-6">
            <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold">Privacy policy: Jeeves YouTube</h1>
            <p class="text-sm text-dark-text-muted">Last updated 30 September 2026</p>

            <p>
                Jeeves YouTube is a private tool that Ben Greenberg built and runs for his own YouTube channel,
                @hummusonrails. It is not offered to anyone else, and only Ben's own Google account signs in to it.
            </p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold pt-4">What it accesses</h2>
            <p>With Ben's permission, through Google's YouTube APIs, the app:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
                <li>reads the channel's videos and their public details (titles, descriptions, view and like counts);</li>
                <li>reads YouTube Analytics reports for the channel (views, watch time, traffic sources, audience retention, impressions);</li>
                <li>uploads videos, thumbnails and captions that Ben has approved, and updates their details.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold pt-4">How the data is used and stored</h2>
            <p>
                The data is used only to show Ben how his channel is doing and to publish his own videos. It is
                stored on Ben's own computer. It is never sold, shared with anyone, used for advertising, or used to
                train AI models. The app does not access any other Google data.
            </p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold pt-4">Removing access</h2>
            <p>
                Access can be removed at any time at
                <a class="modern-link" href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>.
                The app's use of YouTube data follows the
                <a class="modern-link" href="https://www.youtube.com/t/terms">YouTube Terms of Service</a> and the
                <a class="modern-link" href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a>.
            </p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold pt-4">Contact</h2>
            <p>Questions: <a class="modern-link" href="mailto:bengreenberg@gmail.com">bengreenberg@gmail.com</a>.</p>
        </article>
    </div>
</RootLayout>
